<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pallantia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pallantia was the chief town of the Vaccaei, a Celtiberian people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a> basin, on the site of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palencia">Palencia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. It resisted Roman attacks several times in the 2nd century BCE, including a siege by Lucullus in 151 BCE and another by Marcus Aemilius Lepidus in the 130s BCE. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> it became a town of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> Tarraconensis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pallantia.jpg" alt="Pallantia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fernando Pascullo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palencia_Cathedral_2023_-_South_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
